{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Korah took.</b> This matter was in the wilderness of Sinai, when the firstborn were replaced and the Levites were set apart, for Israel thought that Moses our master acted of his own knowledge to give greatness to his brother, also to the sons of Kohath who are close to him, and to all the sons of Levi who are of his family. And the Levites conspired against him because they were given to Aaron and his sons, and Dathan and Abiram conspired because he removed the birthright from Reuben their father and gave it to Joseph. Perhaps they suspected him on account of Joshua his minister. Also Korah was a firstborn, for so it is written. And the standard of Reuben encamped in the south, and Korah in the south of the Tabernacle, for he is of the sons of Kohath. And 'these, princes of the congregation' (Numbers 16:2) were firstborn, and they were the ones offering the burnt offerings; therefore they took fire-pans. And the proof for this interpretation is the sign of the staff, which all Israel saw, that HaShem chose the tribe of Levi in place of the firstborn; therefore it is written, 'and their complaint was ended' (Numbers 17:24 [6]), for the complaint was about this. Also Moses said, 'not from my heart' (Numbers 16:28), because they suspected him that he did it from his own heart, and further, 'nor has HaShem sent me' (Numbers 16:28) in this mission, for all Israel had already believed in him. And further, a conclusive proof: 'all the congregation, every one of them, are holy' (Numbers 16:3) — and this hints at the firstborn, who are holy, for so it is written, 'Sanctify to me every firstborn' (Exodus 13:2), and they were the priests who draw near to HaShem, and they are the essence of the whole congregation." "<b>And Korah took.</b> Men, in elliptical fashion, like 'a donkey [carrying] bread' and many like this. And Rabbi Yonah said that the meaning of ויקח is 'took' in the sense of rising up against someone."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:59.677582453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}